.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-harness-vm-destroy - Destroy a harness VM and prove it is gone


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge harness vm destroy <target-id> <vmid> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Destroy a harness VM this run created, purging it and its unreferenced
disks, then prove it is gone from PVE's own JSON (the destroy task ended OK,
the VMID is free cluster-wide, and the pool no longer lists it). Reuses
VMDestroy's fail-closed status-gated stop before the destroy. The VMID must
be listed in this run's created-VM ledger (--created-file or
$HARNESS_CREATED_FILE) — an unconditional gate — and the destroy must be
confirmed with --yes. Exits non-zero if the gone-proof fails.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--created-file\fP=""
	path to this run's created-VM ledger (default $HARNESS_CREATED_FILE)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for destroy

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--pool\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness pool a VM must be a member of

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)

.PP
\fB--tag\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness tag a VM must carry

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	confirm this irreversible destroy (required; does NOT bypass the created-by-this-run ledger gate)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-harness-vm(1)\fP
